{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Recorded receipt fb14e70f60a3456eae7774eb6e005e69, the repeat of the VerifyLeader end-to-end experiment from its retained inputs. The trigger reproduced the finding: with one of three voters and both non-voters reachable, the leader verified itself at 0 ms after the partition while its successor was elected and applied the new value at 2373 ms, the old leader still held the initial value before the heal, its later verification failed with 'node is not the leader', and no stale verified read was recorded. The control, with the non-voters cut as well, failed verification after 994 ms with 'leadership lost while committing log' while its successor applied the new value at 1917 ms. The account keeps its violated conclusion and asserted defect claim and now records that the bound reproduces on a second execution with a successor roughly 190 ms faster than the first run, so the false success stays confined to the interval between the partition and the lease-driven step-down rather than depending on one run's timing. The counterevidence entry about that bound and the timing limitation are updated with the new numbers, the joint history notes that this is a repeat of the same fixed experiment sharing case names, admissions and assertions, and both VerifyLeader knowledge entries gain the receipt, knowledge-0 on the trigger result and knowledge-1 on the control result.\"}"}}
